# Pinned `spec` revision the conformance runner validates against.
#
# The runner refuses to run if the spec checkout it is given is not at this
# commit (override with --allow-spec-drift when deliberately testing against
# unreleased vocabulary). Without a pin the suite silently tracks whatever is
# on spec `main`, so a run that passed yesterday can pass today for a
# different reason.
#
# To re-pin: check out the new spec revision, put its full SHA and its
# VOCAB_VERSIONS line below, run `make -C . conformance` (or
# `scripts/run_conformance.py`), and record the resulting counts in the PR.

# Pinned at the MERGE commit of jayostis/spec PR #53 on `main`
# (core v3.13 / health v2.9 / clinical v1.20 / coverage v1.9 / checkup v3.5 /
# pots v1.5).
#
# `repo=` IS STILL THE FORK, and still deliberately. This commit is not on
# the-cascade-protocol/spec and is not an ancestor of its `main`. CI clones
# `repo=` and checks out `commit=`, so naming the org here would fail before a
# single fixture ran. Move `repo=` back to the org in the same commit that
# re-pins to an org SHA, once this vocabulary lands there.
#
# WHAT KEEPS THIS COMMIT REACHABLE, because a branch tip is not a guarantee:
# SIX tags point at this exact SHA -- `vocab/core-v3.13`, `vocab/health-v2.9`,
# `vocab/clinical-v1.20`, `vocab/coverage-v1.9`, `vocab/checkup-v3.5` and
# `vocab/pots-v1.5` -- verified with `git ls-remote` before pinning. All six
# releases landed in one commit (jayostis/spec@9f1a55d) inside PR #53, so all
# six tags point at the merge rather than at six distinct commits; that is a
# deliberate choice, not an oversight -- see jayostis/spec#54, which the six
# releases sat untagged and unpinnable behind until it tagged them. A tag holds
# the object even if the fork's `main` is later reset or rebased onto
# upstream, which is the normal end of a fork workflow and would otherwise
# leave every CI run -- including runs of unrelated PRs -- dying at
# `git checkout` on an object that has been garbage-collected. Do not re-pin
# to a fork SHA that no tag points at.
#
# ALL SIX VOCABULARIES MOVE ONE MINOR VERSION, and NO SHAPE FILE CHANGED.
# jayostis/spec#50's scope says "No shapes" and lists every `*.shapes.ttl` as
# do-not-touch; the diff for PR #53 confirms it -- none of the ten
# `*.shapes.ttl` files appears in it. The change is `cascade:RecordClass`, a
# new marker class carried directly by the 83 stable-vocabulary classes (127
# counting the five drafts) that hold record data, replacing a reading of
# `rdfs:subClassOf prov:Entity` that jayostis/spec#34 (ASK-05) ruled out as
# PROV-O alignment rather than a "this is stored data" claim. Also in this
# release: `clinical:CoverageRecord` now names `coverage:InsurancePlan` as its
# successor in a triple (previously only `rdfs:seeAlso` to `fhir:Coverage`),
# and twelve record classes that had no JSON-LD name gain one in
# `contexts/v1/`.
#
# WHAT MOVING THE PIN DID: nothing, to any fixture's verdict. Constraint
# verdicts come from shapes, and no shape moved.
#
#   old pin 3362861 : 151 passed / 26 failed / 177 total
#   new pin e77ba5e : 151 passed / 26 failed / 0 skipped / 177 total
#
# The 26 failures are the same 26 (fixture, reason) pairs KNOWN_FAILURES.json
# already carried at the old pin; asserted, not assumed -- see the PR
# description for the pairwise diff. No entry is added and none is removed.
# Only the file's `specPin` scalar advances, which check_baseline.py requires
# and refuses to run without.
#
# 63,817 constraint checks at BOTH pins, unchanged -- the expected result of
# an ontology-and-context-only release with an identical shape corpus.
#
# WHAT REACHES NO FIXTURE, named here rather than left implied. Every class
# that gains `cascade:RecordClass` in this release is either already exercised
# by an existing fixture (the marker adds no new constraint, so it changes no
# verdict) or is one of the classes `KNOWN_FAILURES.json` and the "Known gaps"
# section of CLAUDE.md already track as UNSHAPED. The marker itself carries no
# SHACL constraint anywhere, so this suite cannot observe it directly at all;
# it is visible here only as a subclass-axiom count, which this runner does
# not measure.

repo=https://github.com/jayostis/spec
commit=e77ba5e8004bf57f34d42a1bee69d1cfb95f86e3
vocab=core=3.13 health=2.9 clinical=1.20 coverage=1.9 checkup=3.5 pots=1.5
